Command:
  c2c poll-inbox

Actual:
  c2c: internal error, uncaught exception:
       Unix.Unix_error(Unix.EROFS, "open", "/home/xertrov/.c2c/repos/8fef2c369975/broker/019f0d62-c446-7e12-9d16-1730159fe21a.inbox.lock")

Context:
  c2c whoami returned session_id 019f0d62-c446-7e12-9d16-1730159fe21a with no registered alias. The current Codex sandbox can read the workspace but cannot write under /home/xertrov/.c2c, so poll-inbox attempted to create/open the inbox lock in a read-only broker path and crashed with an uncaught exception.

Expected:
  poll-inbox should handle EROFS/EACCES on broker lock or inbox paths gracefully. It should return a structured error and actionable guidance, e.g. broker root is not writable in this sandbox, set C2C_MCP_BROKER_ROOT to a writable path or run from a managed session with writable broker state. It should not print an OCaml uncaught exception.